// Typecheck-only project: the SAME sources as tsconfig.json PLUS the test files
// and fixtures that one excludes, with no emit.
//
// Why the split. tsconfig.json is the BUILD, and its exclude is there so test
// files never land in dist — a real constraint, and the reason "just delete the
// exclude" is not the fix. But it meant tsc never looked at a test file at all,
// so a fixture could drift out of the shape it claims and no gate noticed. That
// is the same failure mode as the hand-rolled test doubles that pattern-matched
// on argument shape and silently stopped observing: nothing red, nothing to see,
// coverage that isn't there. `pnpm typecheck` points HERE.
//
// noUncheckedIndexedAccess is OFF, and only here. Every src file is still
// compiled with it ON by `pnpm build`, which runs first in both `pnpm typecheck`
// and CI — this project cannot weaken that. What it drops is `rows[0]` being
// `T | undefined` inside a test, which is ~600 assertions' worth of `!` and no
// signal: a test that indexes past the end fails loudly the moment it runs. The
// errors worth having here are SHAPE errors (a property that doesn't exist, an
// argument that doesn't fit), and those are unaffected.
//
// `exclude` below is the debt, not the design. Each entry is a test file that
// does not typecheck yet; the list is expected to SHRINK and never grow. A new
// test file is covered from birth — you have to add a line to opt out, and that
// line is a thing a reviewer can see.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": []
}
